# Flask module patterns

## New blueprint

```python
from flask import Blueprint, render_template, redirect, request, url_for
from functools import wraps
from database_enhanced import get_user_by_session

my_bp = Blueprint(
    "my_module",
    __name__,
    template_folder="templates",
    static_folder="static",          # optional
    static_url_path="/my-module/static",
)
```

Register in `app.py`: import blueprint, then `app.register_blueprint(my_bp)`.

## Auth decorator

Reuse the `login_required` pattern: read `session_token` cookie, call `get_user_by_session`, redirect to `auth.login_page` on failure.

## File layout

- `routes.py` — HTTP handlers only
- `logic.py` / `config.py` — business logic and constants
- `templates/` — Jinja HTML
- `static/` — module-specific CSS/JS when not shared

## Data access

- PM SQLite: `db/runtime.py` (`connect_pm_db`, `connect_metadata`)
- Paths: `sync_config.py`
- Shared radio logic: `core/radio/`

Do not import from `huawei_params/`; use `core/cm_extractor/huawei_param_dict.py` for dictionary access.
